WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:05.109
ONE OF TONIGHT'S DOCUMENTARY
FEATURE NOMINEES, ALEXANDER

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:10.349
MANUELA, CALLS HIS APPROACH
OBSERVATIONAL STORYTELLING,

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:13.139
WHICH SEEMS LIKE A REALLY
GOOD DEFINITION OF WHAT

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:16.129
A DOCUMENTARY SHOULD BE.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:19.630
THEIR IMPACT CAN BE
EXTRAORDINARY, WHETHER IT'S A

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:24.770
FULL LENGTH FEATURE FILM, OR A
CELL PHONE VIDEO TAKEN BY A

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:29.180
YOUNG WOMAN IN MINNEAPOLIS BY
THE NAME OF DARNELLA FRAZIER

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.980
THAT BECAME THE
CATALYST FOR CHANGE.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.856
HERE ARE THE NOMINEES FOR
DOCUMENTARY FEATURE.

00:00:40.053 --> 00:00:43.970
“COLLECTIVE,” ALEXANDER NANAU
AND BIANCA OANA.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:49.010
“CRIP CAMP,” NICOLE NEWNHAM,
JIM LEBRECHT, AND SARA BOLDER.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:53.450
"THE MOLE AGENT,” MAITE
ALBERDI AND MARCELA SANTIBANEZ.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.810
“MY OCTOPUS TEACHER,”
PIPPA EHRLICH, JAMES REED,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.180
AND CRAIG FOSTER.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.068
“TIME,” GARRETT BRADLEY,
LAUREN DOMINO, AND KELLEN QUINN.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.075
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:01:16.765 --> 00:01:18.630
“MY OCTOPUS TEACHER,”

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.783
PIPPA EHRLICH, JAMES REED,
AND CRAIG FOSTER.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:35.702
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:02:01.319 --> 00:02:03.834
THANK YOU TO THE ACADEMY.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:06.229
AND THANK YOU TO ALL OF OUR

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:09.579
INCREDIBLE NOMINEES WHO SPENT
SO MANY YEARS, AND I PRESUME,

00:02:09.579 --> 00:02:14.150
A LOT OF TEARS, MAKING BEAUTIFUL
AND IMPORTANT FILMS

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.739
AND BRINGING THEM INTO THE WORLD.

00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:23.220
I'D LIKE TO THANK CRAIG FOSTER
AND HIS FAMILY,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:28.239
ESPECIALLY TOM AND SWATI,
WHO OPENED THEIR HEARTS

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:30.909
AND SUPPORTED US EVERY
STEP OF THE WAY AND FED US

00:02:30.909 --> 00:02:37.110
AND ALLOWED THEIR HOME TO BECOME
A PRODUCTION COMPANY FOR THREE YEARS.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:41.829
I WANT TO THANK OUR PRODUCTION
PARTNERS AT OFF THE FENCE,

00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:45.049
ESPECIALLY ELLEN WINDEMUTH
AND SAM BARTON-HUMPHREYS,

00:02:45.049 --> 00:02:49.980
WHO BELIEVED IN THIS FILM
BEFORE IT WAS ANYTHING.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.180
WE WANT TO THANK NETFLIX
FOR ENABLING US TO SHARE

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.370
OUR STORY WITH THE WORLD.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:02.120
AND THEN OUR INCREDIBLE “OCTOPUS”
TEAM WHOSE ARMS STRETCH

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:09.930
ACROSS THE PLANET FROM SOUTH AFRICA
TO AMSTERDAM TO THE U.K. TO THE U.S.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.400
ROGER AND WARREN FOR BEAUTIFUL
CINEMATOGRAPHY.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.910
DAN AND JINX FOR INCREDIBLE
PATIENCE AND EDITING.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:23.250
KEVIN AND BARRY AND KYLE
AND ALL THE PEOPLE AT THE REFINERY.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.860
AND THE INCREDIBLE
SEA CHANGE PROJECT,

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.920
WHO’S BEEN IN THE BACKGROUND
SUPPORTING US THE WHOLE WAY ALONG

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.340
AND CARING SO MUCH FOR THE GREAT
AFRICAN SEA FOREST,

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.260
WHICH IS WHERE THE OCTOPUS LIVED.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.129
AND OUR FRIENDS AND FAMILY
WHO PUT UP WITH YEARS

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:43.870
AND YEARS OF TUNNEL VISION.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:50.290
IF, IN MANY, AND I KNOW THERE ARE MANY
SOUTH AFRICANS WHO ARE AWAKE

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:56.030
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE NIGHT TO WATCH
THE CEREMONY, AND IN MANY WAYS,

00:03:56.030 --> 00:04:00.829
THIS REALLY IS A TINY, PERSONAL STORY
THAT PLAYED OUT IN A SEA FOREST

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:05.150
AT THE VERY TIP OF AFRICA,
BUT ON A MORE UNIVERSAL LEVEL,

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:09.659
I HOPE THAT IT PROVIDED A GLIMPSE
OF A DIFFERENT KIND OF RELATIONSHIP

00:04:09.659 --> 00:04:12.652
BETWEEN HUMAN BEINGS
AND THE NATURAL WORLD.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:19.388
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU. AND I DON'T HAVE
A LOT TO ADD TO THAT.

00:04:19.388 --> 00:04:22.670
PIPPA, YOU COVERED IT VERY WELL.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:27.450
IT'S A GREAT AND TOTALLY
OVERWHELMING HONOR TO BE HERE.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.380
AND SO THANK YOU SO MUCH
TO THE ACADEMY AND ALL THE

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.190
INCREDIBLE FILMS THAT
WERE IN OUR CATEGORY.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.700
IT'S REALLY HUMBLING
AND AMAZING.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:43.880
AND I'D ALSO LIKE TO THANK
MY FAMILY, ROSIE AND ISABEL,

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:48.530
AND MY MOM AND MY TWO SISTERS,
JENNY AND JANICE.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.750
I DON'T THINK I'D BE HERE TODAY
WITHOUT THEIR SORT OF LEVEL

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.010
OF LOVE AND SUPPORT,
SO THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.960
AND I THINK THE FINAL EXTRA
THANK YOU FOR CRAIG,

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.340
WHO, WHILE IT WAS SUCH
AN ENORMOUS TEAM MAKING

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.310
THIS FILM IN THE END,
IT SORT OF BEGAN AND ENDED WITH HIM,

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.970
AND IT’S HIS STORY.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.000
AND HE KIND OF SHOWED US THAT

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.940
YOU KNOW, IF A MAN CAN KIND OF FORM
A FRIENDSHIP WITH AN OCTOPUS,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.590
IT DOES SORT OF MAKE YOU WONDER
WHAT ELSE IS POSSIBLE.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:21.190
SO THANK YOU, CRAIG,
AND CHEERS, EVERYONE

